-- title:
--   An order-three quotient character
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be an abelian group. Let $L\le G$ and $a,d,h\in G$, with $a,h\in L$, $d\notin L$, $2h=0$, $3d\in\{0,h\}$, and $\langle a,d,h\rangle=G$. There is an additive character $$\chi:G\longrightarrow\mathbb Z/3,\qquad\chi(a)=\chi(h)=0,\quad\chi(d)=1.$$
--
--   This supplies a constructive quotient coordinate without assuming $G$ finite.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, https://github.com/alexcour/couret-finite-verifications/blob/65b828d9ffd016ce2a1b05403f303fa5f948c10f/research/correspondants_20261013/lean/CayleyTwoColourAbelian.lean#L559-L669, lines 559–669; source file SHA-256 c9643d6e3a677d5a903623825d50a309d87175a21ace2b7ab56939d9189f13b1; theorem Couret.CayleyDoublet.abelianThreeCharacter_of_generation

